Description: Implements principal-stratification methods for estimating
    time-specific and pooled heterogeneous treatment effects in longitudinal
    studies where outcomes may be truncated by death. An explicit mapping is
    the sole source of truth for structural columns, baseline and cutoff times,
    prediction-model covariates, effect modifiers, and continuous or binary
    outcome type. The propensity-score, principal-score, and outcome-prediction
    functions refit and predict independently on every call and do not create
    shared fitted-model state. Time-specific estimation accepts an explicit set
    of target times, while pooled estimation always uses every observed time
    from baseline through cutoff. The package also provides subject-level
    bootstrap inference, balance diagnostics, principal-stratum summaries,
    treatment-group-specific odds-ratio estimation, and sensitivity analysis.
